Maintenance
===========

Read this before assuming any part of the backend is finished. Items are
ordered by how much damage ignoring them causes.


Correctness gaps
----------------

1. Quest claiming has no completion record and no idempotency guard.
   POST /quest/:id/claim looks up the quest, adds quest.xp to the user, and
   returns. Nothing records that the user claimed it, nothing checks whether
   the quest is in today's set, and nothing prevents the same call being made
   a hundred times. A student with the endpoint can mint unlimited XP.

   The fix is a quest_completions table keyed unique on (userId, questId,
   dateKey), written in the same transaction as the XP increment, with the
   claim rejected if the quest is not in resolveDailyQuests(today).

2. The same handler emits quests:pointsgranted to all students for one
   student's claim. It should be emit.toUser.

3. Quest badges are never evaluated. services/badges/questBadges.ts exports
   evaluateQuestBadges and has no call site. Once (1) is fixed it should be
   called from the claim handler, inside the same transaction.

4. Challenge podium badges are never settled.
   services/badges/challengeBadges.ts exports settleChallengePositionBadges
   and nothing calls it. Podium badge rows are created with the challenge, so
   the data is there; what is missing is the moment of settlement when a
   challenge ends. There is no scheduler in the project, so this needs either
   a cron entry hitting an admin endpoint or a lazy settle on the first read
   of a finished challenge.

5. challenges.participantsCount is denormalised and only maintained on the
   register path. Any other write to challenge_participants leaves it stale.


Legacy and duplication
----------------------

* user_stats holds xp, currentStreak and longestStreak that nothing
  authoritative reads. Streak and level are derived in meController from
  session history and users.totalXp. Either backfill and start using the
  table or drop it; leaving it half-alive invites someone to read the wrong
  number.

* Two activity ledgers exist. exercise_sessions is what every user-facing
  read path uses. activity_logs belongs to the older points-per-unit Activity
  catalogue and is written only by the award-points endpoint. Decide which
  survives before adding features to either.

* Two activity catalogues exist for the same reason: activities
  (points-per-unit) and activity_areas plus activity_sub_activities (the
  facility tree the app browses). They are not joined.


